Cell["\<\
Here is the histogram of the historical data of daily return of a given index. 
The first few sample cumulants are evaluated and are used to determine the \
parameter of option pricing models. 
The probability density functions under the Black-Scholes model (red line) \
and Merton\[CloseCurlyQuote]s jump diffusion model (blue line) are shown as \
well. 

The given index in the first line can be changed, and this program still \
works. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.540556122106698*^9, 3.540556187261425*^9}, {
  3.540556224712567*^9, 3.5405562264626665`*^9}, {3.540556258653508*^9, 
  3.5405565784447994`*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

